Build fixes for the CoreText backend with GCC on old SDKs.

CoreText is a sub-framework of ApplicationServices before macOS 10.8, so
<CoreText/CoreText.h> is not found there; include the ApplicationServices
umbrella in pangocoretext.h (as hb-coretext.h does) and let the .c files
get CoreText through pangocoretext-private.h.
pangocoretext.h: also declare bzero() before the system headers; with GCC
and the 10.6 SDK it was used undeclared (upstream 1.58.1 added the same
include to pangocoretext-fontmap.c).
pangocoretext-private.h: duplicate declaration, an error under
-Werror=redundant-decls.
pangocoretext.c: PangoCoreTextFontMap* assigned to PangoFontMap*, an error
with GCC 14+.
pangocoretext-fontmap.c: redundant static declarations (G_DEFINE_TYPE
already declares them, -Werror=redundant-decls); string literals in a
non-const array; CTFontCopyDefaultCascadeListForLanguages is 10.8+, fall
back to the font's kCTFontCascadeListAttribute on older SDKs.
